First Author: Ding
Title: Machine learning-based prediction of high hospital charges after lung transplantation in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease patients
Source number: 62

Very short summary: This retrospective study used 1,159 adult lung-transplant hospitalizations from the US Nationwide Inpatient Sample between 2005 and 2014 to predict whether total hospital charges were in the highest 20% of the cohort. Six machine-learning models were evaluated using a 70:30 internal split and ten-fold cross-validation for training and tuning; the Gradient Boosting Machine was selected as the optimal model, achieving a test-set AUC of 0.8078, accuracy of 81.64%, and F1-score of 0.6773.

