	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Missing Race and Zip-Code Income Quartile values were imputed using Multiple Imputation by Chained Equations with a Gradient Boosting Classifier for multiclass categorical imputation. Seven post-discharge or manually coded variables were excluded to reduce information leakage, and feature selection reduced the model to 27 variables. High-cost cases represented approximately 20% of the cohort, but no resampling, class weighting, or other explicit imbalance treatment was reported. The exact training count was not stated; the GBM test confusion matrix contains 348 observations. Source code and trained model weights were not reported.

