	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The outcome was high-cost hospitalization, defined as total hospital charges at or above the cohort’s 80th percentile ($600,223.40). On the held-out test set, GBM achieved AUC 0.8078, accuracy 0.8164, precision 0.6944, recall 0.6657, and F1-score 0.6773. No AUC confidence interval, explicitly reported specificity, or NPV was provided. Calibration curves were presented, and GBM had a Brier score of 0.1360. Decision-curve analysis was not reported.

